# courses-medicine.kb - Courses / Medicine
# Format: concept | intent | answer | keywords | patterns | tl | bis
# 4 entries, one genuinely distinct fact per line.

medicine | definition | Medicine is the science and practice of diagnosing and treating disease, and the degree is long because it combines several years of scientific study with years of unsupervised practice afterwards. The Philippines route is four years of medicine after a nursing or science degree, then a further year of internship before the board exam and the licence. What the course actually teaches is differential diagnosis, which is ranking the possible causes rather than recognising the one obvious illness. | medicine, doctor, diagnose, disease, degree, internship | what is medicine, how long to become a doctor, is medicine hard | medicine | medisina
residency | definition | A residency is supervised postgraduate training done after the medical degree, and it is where a doctor becomes a specialist. It is intense for a reason that is easy to miss from outside: the hours are long because the ward is staffed by trainees, and the supervision exists to catch the errors that experience would otherwise catch. In the Philippines it runs for three to four years in most specialisations, and the return is access to consultant posts rather than a guaranteed one. | residency, training, specialist, supervision, ward, consultant | what is a residency, how long is residency, is residency worth it | residency | residency
differential diagnosis | definition | Differential diagnosis is the process of listing the possible causes of a presentation and then ranking them, and it is the core skill in medicine rather than recognising diseases. A good differential is common things first, serious things not forgotten, and matched to the findings actually present rather than to the whole textbook. The failures are diagnostic momentum, where the first plausible explanation is kept because it fits, and premature closure, where the search stops once something explains the symptoms. | differential diagnosis, list, cause, rank, presentation, symptom | what is differential diagnosis, how do doctors diagnose, what is diagnostic momentum | differential diagnosis | diagnosis
medical school | definition | A medical school is the institution that gives the degree which, with the licensure exam, entitles somebody to practise as a doctor. The curriculum is built around the sciences first, since the clinical years assume them, and the teaching in those early years is largely about the structure of the body and how it works when well. A common regret among graduates is that the amount of time spent on the body outnumbers the amount spent on the person, which is a design choice rather than an accident. | medical school, degree, doctor, licence, science, clinical | how do i get into medical school, is medical school hard, what do you learn in medical school | medical school | paaralan ng medisina
